approve Plugin for DokuWiki

Page approval mechanism for dokuwiki.

All documentation for this plugin can be found at
https://www.dokuwiki.org/plugin:approve

If you install this plugin manually, make sure it is installed in
lib/plugins/approve/ - if the folder is called different it
will not work!

Please refer to http://www.dokuwiki.org/plugins for additional info
on how to install plugins in DokuWiki.

Remote API: plugin.approve.getLatestApprovedRevision(page) requires read access.
JSON-RPC and XML-RPC return an object/struct with a boolean found field. When
found is false, no approved revision exists (including pages outside the
plugin's scope). When true, rev and approved are integer Unix timestamps,
approved_by is a string, and version is an integer if available; otherwise
version is omitted. Missing pages and denied access produce RPC errors.
This replaces the earlier experimental null-based response contract.

Run the standalone database and access checks with:
php tests/latest-approved.php

To test both actual RPC endpoints against a deployed test wiki, set
APPROVE_RPC_TOKEN to a read-only bearer token and APPROVE_RPC_FIXTURES to the
path of a JSON fixture file, then run python3 tests/rpc-integration.py.
See tests/rpc-fixtures.example.json. The file contains base_url and cases:
approved, unapproved, without_version, hidden, denied, and missing. Each case has page and either expected (the exact RPC
object, with numeric timestamps) or error (a substring of the RPC fault).
The without_version page must be approved with a NULL database version; denied
must exist but be unreadable by the token. Keep credentials out of the file.

